# UI theme (GEAR look)

When editing menus, overlays, sheets, or dialogs under `lib/ui/`:

1. Follow **`docs/UI_THEME.md`** (reference = GEAR inventory sheet).
2. **Phone-first / portrait only** — assume ~360–430 px width; finger taps. Do not ship desktop-only hover UX.
3. Prefer **`MenuChrome`** + **`GameTheme`** primitives — do not invent new colors/radii.
4. Titles → `GameTheme.menuTitle`; sections → `MenuChrome.sectionLabel`; lists → `cardBox` / `listCard`.
5. Multi-tab overlays → `MenuChrome.tabRail` (same as GEAR/BAG/TOOLS).
6. Actions → `KenneyButton` (brown / grey / red). No Material `TextButton` in forge dialogs.
7. Press Start (`GameTheme.pixel`) only for combat HUD and tiny tags — not menu titles.
8. Skip restyling: combat HUD, bottom nav, start menu, hub world-path scene. Item tooltips: phone long-press + compact bag compare (see `item_tooltip.dart`).

English in-game copy. If you add a new shared chrome helper, put it on `MenuChrome` and mention it in `docs/UI_THEME.md`.
